q00059,b0162,815535,1,27,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/815535,"It’s as though you were pointing a gun at my head. It’s just a way of getting somebody to say something they probably don’t mean. What else can I say, or anybody say, but, ‘I love you too’?",,,
q00060,b0162,815535,1,28,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/815535,"Yes, and Eliza and I composed a precocious critique of the Constitution of the United Staes of America, too. We argued that it was a good scheme for misery as any, since its success in keeping the common people reasonably happy and proud depended on the strength of the people themselves-- and yet it described no practical machinery which would tend to make the people, as opposed to their elected representatives, strong.",,,
q00061,b0162,815535,1,29,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/815535,"My brother said this to him, tapping his own forehead with his fingertips: “If you think this laboratory is bad, you should see what it’s like in here.” And so on. ***",,,
q00062,b0201,2756256,1,0,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2756256,"...there are people who try to look as if they are doing a good and thorough job, and then there are the people who actually damn well do it, for its own sake.",,,
q00063,b0201,2756256,1,1,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2756256,"There can be a habit of love, I think. You justify the way you are living by telling yourself that love leaves you no other choice. And so you are into love. Women stay with dreadful men. You see it all the time. You wonder why. You know they are wasting their lives. You know they are worth far more than what they have. But they stay on and on. They grow old staying on and on. They say it is love so often to themselves, it does become love.",,,
q00064,b0201,2756256,1,2,https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2756256,"A lot of my motivation had been to show him that I had value, that I was valued by the world, and so I was worthy of his love and his respect. He had never shown me love or respect.",,,
